{
  "version": 1,
  "note": [
    "The Android client's input wire format, pinned from both sides.",
    "Kotlin: apk/app/src/test/java/com/remotedexter/InputJsonContractTest.kt asserts",
    "        InputJson produces these commands.",
    "Rust:   modules/module10/tests/android_wire_contract.rs asserts the host's own",
    "        serde derives accept them and reject everything in must_not_parse.",
    "Neither side imports the other. The file is the contract; drift on either",
    "side turns that side's suite red instead of failing silently on a device.",
    "Block 11 added TextInput. The phone sends TEXT, not scan codes: a scan code names a physical key position and only the host knows which position produces which character, so the mapping lives in module10::keymap and the wire carries what the user actually typed.",
    "2026-08-30: added the three scroll cases. MouseScroll is NOT a new wire message - the host has accepted and injected it since Block 7, coarse detents and hi-res, both axes. What was missing was any client that sent one: two fingers went to onZoomPan, marked 'no host traffic', so a swipe moved the rendered picture and never left the phone. This is a builder joining a message that was already contracted on the Rust side. Lines rather than Pixels because a two-finger swipe has already been quantised into detents by the time it reaches the wire, and sending pixels would mean inventing a hi-res figure this path does not have."
  ],
